text":"Read twice and referred to the Committee on Banking, Housing, and Urban Affairs."},"laws":[],"number":"1124","originChamber":"Senate","policyArea":"Finance and Financial Sector","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"C001098","district":null,"fullName":"Sen. Cruz, Ted [R-TX]","party":"R","state":"TX"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-03-25","actionDesc":"Introduced in Senate","text":"<p><strong>Anti-CBDC Surveillance State Act&nbsp; </strong></p><p>This bill prohibits a Federal Reserve bank from offering products or services directly to an individual, maintaining an account on behalf of an individual, or issuing a central bank digital currency (i.e., a digital dollar). Further, the Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System is prohibited from using a central bank digital currency to implement monetary policy or from testing, studying, creating, or implementing a central bank digital currency, with exceptions as provided by the bill.</p>","updateDate":"2026-01-15T22:47:24Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Anti-CBDC Surveillance State Act","type":"s","updateDate":"2026-05-12T11:03:31Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-05-12T11:03:31Z"}
